{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018XWABD544AqNRpeoJeeUWK","type":"tool_result","content":"1\timport Mathlib\n2\t\n3\topen Topology Filter Matrix\n4\t\n5\t/--\n6\tLet $F:\\mathbb{R}^2 \\to \\mathbb{R}$ and $g:\\mathbb{R} \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be twice continuously differentiable functions with the following properties:\n7\t\\begin{itemize}\n8\t\\item $F(u,u)=0$ for every $u \\in \\mathbb{R}$;\n9\t\\item for every $x \\in \\mathbb{R}$, $g(x)>0$ and $x^2g(x) \\leq 1$;\n10\t\\item for every $(u,v) \\in \\mathbb{R}^2$, the vector $\\nabla F(u,v)$ is either $\\mathbf{0}$ or parallel to the vector $\\langle g(u),-g(v) \\rangle$.\n11\t\\end{itemize}\n12\tProve that there exists a constant $C$ such that for every $n \\geq 2$ and any $x_1,\\dots,x_{n+1} \\in \\mathbb{R}$, we have $\\min_{i \\neq j} |F(x_i,x_j)| \\leq \\frac{C}{n}$.\n13\t-/\n14\ttheorem putnam_2011_a5\n15\t(F : (Fin 2 → ℝ) → ℝ)\n16\t(g : ℝ → ℝ)\n17\t(vec : ℝ → ℝ → (Fin 2 → ℝ))\n18\t(Fgrad : (Fin 2 → ℝ) → (Fin 2 → ℝ))\n19\t(parallel : (Fin 2 → ℝ) → (Fin 2 → ℝ) → Prop)\n20\t(hparallel : parallel = (fun u v : Fin 2 → ℝ => ∃ c : ℝ, u = c • v))\n21\t(Fgdiff : ContDiff ℝ 2 F ∧ ContDiff ℝ 2 g)\n22\t(prop1 : ∀ uu : Fin 2 → ℝ, uu 0 = uu 1 → F uu = 0)\n23\t(prop2 : ∀ x : ℝ, g x > 0 ∧ x ^ 2 * g x ≤ 1)\n24\t(hvec : ∀ x y : ℝ, (vec x y) 0 = x ∧ (vec x y) 1 = y)\n25\t(hFgrad : ∀ uv : Fin 2 → ℝ, Fgrad uv 0 = deriv (fun x : ℝ => F (vec x (uv 1))) (uv 0) ∧ Fgrad uv 1 = deriv (fun y : ℝ => F (vec (uv 0) y)) (uv 1))\n26\t(prop3 : ∀ uv : Fin 2 → ℝ, Fgrad uv = 0 ∨ parallel (Fgrad uv) (vec (g (uv 0)) (-g (uv 1))))\n27\t: ∃ C : ℝ, ∀ n ≥ 2, ∀ x : Fin (n + 1) → ℝ, sInf {Fxx : ℝ | ∃ i j : Fin (n + 1), i ≠ j ∧ Fxx = |F (vec (x i) (x j))|} ≤ C / n :=\n28\tsorry\n29\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f42530df-1cb5-421a-a8c6-7979ec175974","uuid":"63f16feb-dee0-4bf6-9c2f-74f83f93631a","timestamp":"2026-10-14T03:44:31.232Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/work/putnam_2011_a5.lean","content":"import Mathlib\n\nopen Topology Filter Matrix\n\n/--\nLet $F:\\mathbb{R}^2 \\to \\mathbb{R}$ and $g:\\mathbb{R} \\to \\mathbb{R}$ be twice continuously differentiable functions with the following properties:\n\\begin{itemize}\n\\item $F(u,u)=0$ for every $u \\in \\mathbb{R}$;\n\\item for every $x \\in \\mathbb{R}$, $g(x)>0$ and $x^2g(x) \\leq 1$;\n\\item for every $(u,v) \\in \\mathbb{R}^2$, the vector $\\nabla F(u,v)$ is either $\\mathbf{0}$ or parallel to the vector $\\langle g(u),-g(v) \\rangle$.\n\\end{itemize}\nProve that there exists a constant $C$ such that for every $n \\geq 2$ and any $x_1,\\dots,x_{n+1} \\in \\mathbb{R}$, we have $\\min_{i \\neq j} |F(x_i,x_j)| \\leq \\frac{C}{n}$.\n-/\ntheorem putnam_2011_a5\n(F : (Fin 2 → ℝ) → ℝ)\n(g : ℝ → ℝ)\n(vec : ℝ → ℝ → (Fin 2 → ℝ))\n(Fgrad : (Fin 2 → ℝ) → (Fin 2 → ℝ))\n(parallel : (Fin 2 → ℝ) → (Fin 2 → ℝ) → Prop)\n(hparallel : parallel = (fun u v : Fin 2 → ℝ => ∃ c : ℝ, u = c • v))\n(Fgdiff : ContDiff ℝ 2 F ∧ ContDiff ℝ 2 g)\n(prop1 : ∀ uu : Fin 2 → ℝ, uu 0 = uu 1 → F uu = 0)\n(prop2 : ∀ x : ℝ, g x > 0 ∧ x ^ 2 * g x ≤ 1)\n(hvec : ∀ x y : ℝ, (vec x y) 0 = x ∧ (vec x y) 1 = y)\n(hFgrad : ∀ uv : Fin 2 → ℝ, Fgrad uv 0 = deriv (fun x : ℝ => F (vec x (uv 1))) (uv 0) ∧ Fgrad uv 1 = deriv (fun y : ℝ => F (vec (uv 0) y)) (uv 1))\n(prop3 : ∀ uv : Fin 2 → ℝ, Fgrad uv = 0 ∨ parallel (Fgrad uv) (vec (g (uv 0)) (-g (uv 1))))\n: ∃ C : ℝ, ∀ n ≥ 2, ∀ x : Fin (n + 1) → ℝ, sInf {Fxx : ℝ | ∃ i j : Fin (n + 1), i ≠ j ∧ Fxx = |F (vec (x i) (x j))|} ≤ C / n :=\nsorry\n","numLines":29,"startLine":1,"totalLines":29}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018XWABD544AqNRpeoJeeUWK","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
